    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field. The audit line above confirms a well-formed value: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` \u2192 REGION `NSW`, FY `27`, HASH8 `16E6609E`, CHK `1`.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** (drives DTO generation): removed the `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, and `membershipNumber` schema blocks; added a `memberId` block; updated the `locality` and `fiscalYear` descriptions to reference the memberId.\n- **`Owner.java`**: renamed the persisted field/column `customerCode`/`customer_code` \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id` with matching getter/setter.\n- **`schema.sql`** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres): renamed the `customer_code` column to `member_id` (widened the VARCHAR to 32 to accommodate the longer id plus any collision suffix).\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`**: removed the `checkDigit` and `membershipNumber` mappings/methods; `memberId` now auto-maps from the entity. `locality` now reads the leading REGION letters of the memberId, and `fiscalYear` reads the two FY digits that follow \u2014 both literally referencing the memberId (via a shared `regionLength` helper). Removed the now-unused `fiscalYearOf`; kept `fiscalEndYear` (still used by membership points).\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**: replaced `customerCode(owner)` with `memberId(owner)`, which builds `REGION + FY + HASH8 + Luhn(REGION+FY+HASH8)` and applies **collision de-duplication against existing `memberId`s**. Added `fiscalYearTwoDigits` and `luhn` helpers. Updated `primaryIdentifier` to return the memberId, and the `OwnerCreatedEvent` audit record's field (`customerCode` \u2192 `memberId`) plus the human-readable audit line, so the **audit record references the memberId**. The **owner segment** references the memberId transitively through the updated `locality`.\n\nThe Luhn algorithm and the SHA-256 HASH8 derivation match the reference implementations in `AcceptanceBase` exactly, and the fiscal-year computation reuses the same \"starts 1 July\" rule as before.",
